  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1952-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The logarithm product rule changes the equation to \\(\\log(pq)=\\log(p+q),\\) so the positive arguments must satisfy \\[ pq=p+q. \\] Therefore \\(p(q-1)=q,\\) giving \\(p=\\frac{q}{q-1}.\\) Its admissible values have \\(q\\gt1,\\) which also keeps all logarithm arguments positive.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the logarithms on the left before equating their positive arguments",
        "Solve \\(pq=p+q\\) for \\(p\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
